  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/2ED47F">Remark <span data-tag="2ED47F">1.1.5.17</span>.</a> It is immediate from the definition that $f: S \rightarrow T$ is a categorical equivalence if and only if $\sCoNerve [S] \rightarrow \sCoNerve [T]$ is an equivalence (of simplicial categories), if and only if $|\sCoNerve [S]| \rightarrow |\sCoNerve [T]|$ is an equivalence (of topological categories). </p>
